vkd3d-shader: read `texture` and `point` as state values in a state block.

**Microsoft's compiler accepts `ColorArg1[0] = texture;` and vkd3d-shader
rejected it with a syntax error**, in 43 of Caribbean Legend's 54 effects:

    balls.fx:12:27: E5000: syntax error, unexpected ';', expecting '('

`texture` is an HLSL keyword (the sampler type), so the lexer returns
KW_TEXTURE and the right-hand side of a state assignment never reaches the
NEW_IDENTIFIER path that turns `modulate` or `selectarg1` into a state
constant. In an effect it means D3DTA_TEXTURE -- `fx_2_colorarg_values` in fx.c
already carries "TEXTURE" -- and `MinFilter[0] = point;` is D3DTEXF_POINT the
same way. The left-hand side already accepts KW_TEXTURE (stateblock_lhs_identifier);
only the value side was missing.

**Recognised in the lexer, not the grammar, because the grammar version
conflicts.** A `state_block_keyword_value` production reached from
complex_initializer produced 73 shift/reduce conflicts; restricted to
`'=' keyword ';'` it still produced one, on KW_TEXTURE against a constructor
`texture(...)`. hlsl.y carries `%expect 1`, and raising that to hide a second
conflict is how a grammar starts parsing things nobody meant. The lexer can ask
the one question that matters with trailing context -- is the keyword followed
directly by `;` -- and only answers differently inside a state block, where
`in_state_block` is already maintained.

Measured with upstream vkd3d master on the build host: 8 / 54 before, 45 / 54
after, no new bison conflicts, and nothing that compiled before stopped
compiling.

diff --git a/libs/vkd3d/libs/vkd3d-shader/hlsl.l b/libs/vkd3d/libs/vkd3d-shader/hlsl.l
index 85f0d89..da62c1b 100644
--- a/libs/vkd3d/libs/vkd3d-shader/hlsl.l
+++ b/libs/vkd3d/libs/vkd3d-shader/hlsl.l
@@ -124,6 +124,25 @@ pass                    {return KW_PASS;                }
 PixelShader             {return KW_PIXELSHADER;         }
 PointStream             {return KW_POINTSTREAM;         }
 pixelshader             {return KW_PIXELSHADER;         }
+point/{WS}*;            |
+texture/{WS}*;          {
+                            struct hlsl_ctx *ctx = yyget_extra(yyscanner);
+
+                            /* Vessel: a keyword standing alone as the value of a
+                             * state assignment is the state constant of that name.
+                             * Microsoft's compiler reads "ColorArg1[0] = texture;"
+                             * as D3DTA_TEXTURE and "MinFilter[0] = point;" as
+                             * D3DTEXF_POINT; the grammar only ever sees the
+                             * keyword and fails "expecting '('". Recognised here
+                             * rather than in hlsl.y because a grammar rule for it
+                             * collides with every declaration that starts with
+                             * the same keyword. Outside a state block it is still
+                             * the keyword. */
+                            if (!ctx->in_state_block)
+                                return yytext[0] == 'p' ? KW_POINT : KW_TEXTURE;
+                            yylval->name = hlsl_strdup(ctx, yytext);
+                            return NEW_IDENTIFIER;
+                        }
 point                   {return KW_POINT;               }
 RasterizerOrderedBuffer           {return KW_RASTERIZERORDEREDBUFFER;            }
 RasterizerOrderedStructuredBuffer {return KW_RASTERIZERORDEREDSTRUCTUREDBUFFER;  }
